@@ readme.formats
# relay

A small token-authenticated message relay.

## Layout

- `src/` wire format and token lifecycle (Rust)
- `web/` session client (TypeScript)
- `tools/` operational scripts (Python)
- `cmd/` relay entrypoint (Go)

## Frame format

Every frame is `varint channel`, `varint length`, then `length` payload bytes.
Frames larger than one mebibyte are rejected before any allocation happens.

## Token lifecycle

Tokens without an expiry are treated as expired. A token is valid when its
subject is known and its deadline has not passed.

@@ config
listen: ":4000"
max_frame_bytes: 1048576
token:
  ttl_seconds: 3600
  clock_skew_seconds: 30

@@ config.rotation
listen: ":4000"
max_frame_bytes: 1048576
token:
  ttl_seconds: 3600
  clock_skew_seconds: 30
  rotation_window_seconds: 300

@@ config.short
listen: ":4000"
max_frame_bytes: 1048576
token:
  ttl_seconds: 900
  clock_skew_seconds: 30
  audit_log: true

